  "RESOLVED
1. kotoba-lang/shell window host now compiles (root cause: `5c39631` added call sites without declarations) — `658dfde`.
2. `--web-url` now mounts a WKWebView, and the runtime forwards it — `658dfde`.
3. `apps/tamaki-observer-web` focus ring now points at `--color-primitive-yellow-300` — `658dfde`. Source only; `dist/style.css` is regenerated by the shadow `:compile-finish` hook, and was left alone because another session had it open.
4. The native chat button posted an empty prompt on every click (`perform` never emitted the `.value` its consumer reads) — `658dfde`.

OPEN
5. cloud-itonami-app: the Worker UI is verified structurally, over HTTP, and as a native WKWebView render of the live app with its real script running and zero JS errors. It has NOT been driven through a completed passkey ceremony, because that needs a real authenticator. Closing this needs a WebAuthn virtual authenticator in the host, not more test coverage.
6. Workspace: `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` reports STALE on plain `origin/main`, independent of any single entry — whole-fleet local-checkout drift, because the generator pins from local working HEADs. Deliberately not addressed: the only way to make it green is the wholesale regeneration that is forbidden. The `--check` signal is therefore not usable as a gate in its current form.
7. Workspace: `manifest/docs-edn-only.cljs verify` fails on four counts, and `md=75` is one of them even though it is not printed as a section — 75 `.md` files still live under `90-docs` against the EDN-only policy, which is a migration decision, not a repair.

   Of the 22 unparseable EDN files, **3 are now fixed** (`METRICS-DEPLOYMENT-COORDINATION-SUMMARY`, `MONTH-3-AUTOMATIC-ROLLBACK-TRIGGERS`, `MONTH-3-PRE-FLIGHT-READINESS-PLAN`) and **19 remain**, plus 7 non-tx-data ADRs and 7 path-md-refs.

   `verify` itself was under-reporting. Its text-level checks (md-path references, source-format residue) sat inside the same `let` as `edn/read-string`, so **a parse error skipped them for that file**. Fixing one parse error appeared to add md-path hits that had in fact always been there. The checks are now independent, which moved path-md-refs from a reported 4 to a true 7. Expect the same for `not-tx` as the remaining 19 parse errors are fixed: that check legitimately needs parsed content, so its total is still a lower bound.

   Two diagnostic scripts were added because the reader message is actively misleading here — it names where the wreckage surfaced, not where it started, often hundreds of lines away:
   - `scripts/docs-edn-parse-report.cljs` — every failing file with its reader error (`verify` caps its listing at 20).
   - `scripts/docs-edn-locate-break.cljs` — the actual defect line. A delimiter-stack scan reports surplus, mismatched and unclosed delimiters with the line that opened them; when delimiters are sound it falls back to prefix-parsing for malformed strings and tokens. No heuristics, so `pr-str` body blobs full of escaped quotes do not false-positive. Diagnoses all 19 in seconds.

   Worth knowing before repairing any of these: `edn/read-string` reads only the first form and **silently ignores trailing text**, so a surplus delimiter at the very end of a file is harmless while one in the middle stays invisible until EOF.

   The 19 were left alone deliberately. Each needs a structural judgement inside a document this work does not own — e.g. `MONTH-3-CANARY-EXECUTION-TIMELINE` has a map opened on line 193 that is never closed across 200+ lines of nested phase maps, and the `}` could correctly go in several places. A fix that parses but nests differently is worse than a loud failure, because the loader nils bad shapes and the document would then be silently wrong instead of silently absent. The three that were fixed were each unambiguous — a dropped `\"`, a dropped `}`, an invalid `80+` literal and a digit-initial keyword name — and the structural one was confirmed by checking the repaired shape (5 risk maps, each with exactly `:risk :likelihood :impact :mitigation`) rather than by assuming.
8. Environment: an orphaned process (`resource-guard run build -- clojure -M:server`, PPID 1) holds the workspace-wide `build` scope lock, so a long-running server blocks every session's builds. Left alone — not this session's process. The underlying flaw is that a server was started under the `build` scope at all.
9. cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-app: the shared west checkout is stuck behind `origin/main` because another session holds uncommitted edits to `web.clj`, `server.clj`, `identity.clj`, `deps.edn` and `core_test.clj` there. Their edits are based on a pre-token-fix tree, so committing them may revert the token fix and worker routes. This is the shared-checkout-direct-edit hazard, and it can only be resolved by that session."
  :adr/verification
  "Re-verified at close against each repo's current default branch, not against the commits this work created — three other sessions landed in cloud-itonami-app meanwhile.

- cloud-itonami-app @ 0e3a5c6: `clojure -M:test` → **56 tests / 321 assertions, 0 failures** (includes worker, worker-http and the design-token guard). `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 10 warnings, **all in other sessions' new files** (mail_sync, bitcoin_wallet, agent_control, account_link_sync), none in files touched here. Every warning is `Unresolved var` — the same call-sites-without-declarations shape that made the shell host uncompilable, so it is worth watching.
- kotoba-lang/shell @ 658dfde: the macOS window host compiles with **0 errors and 0 warnings**. Both native surfaces captured during development: kotoba:dom (regression check) and `--web-url` against both a `file://` page and the live app.
- The Worker surface was rendered in WKWebView with the app's real interaction script running: `web/errors: []`, and the URL advanced to `#settings`, proving `showView` and the view-change hook executed.
- west pins reachable from their child tips: cloud-itonami-app 7113377b (advanced further by another session, this work included), shell 658dfded.

Not verified: a completed passkey ceremony. It needs a real authenticator, so the Worker tab has never been driven while unlocked. Everything behind that gate is covered at the HTTP layer instead."
